#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3817ce70-a3ff-5d76-a92e-d07723b9ee70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529708} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5f285e-8dc0-5c5d-9205-5077e2524a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529850} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4a8876-64da-599a-b333-8da10c7aac94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529960} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a515b3-38b4-574d-ab70-b455f36a3a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530111} {:answer/id #uuid "f91da311-0343-5a45-b221-265ed560e0d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529960} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe95487d-a357-5109-9ec1-41b889997c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e74c735c-6d68-5fb5-ad5e-520e538fc830" :question/math-academy-id "q-146981" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}}{\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}y+y)}{(1+{x}^{2})},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2({1}^{2}\\cdot y+y)}{(1+{1}^{2})}=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a70864-faa5-54be-a449-99d26ac3090c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529611} {:answer/id #uuid "4016d54d-03ed-5d80-9023-2a222b021197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529729} {:answer/id #uuid "421cf42f-466d-5bf8-b694-47753f0f385e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529734} {:answer/id #uuid "abd5352c-5d54-5e3c-8b55-15e577a50730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530008} {:answer/id #uuid "db75dada-7b81-542d-bf6b-9186ddf533e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530008} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cacacfd-fd44-50c7-9618-968db11d920d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "febad6f8-061f-513c-bf3e-fbe38a2e6b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146867" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}-y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2-x-y)}{(\\frac{3}{2}-y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2x-2y}{3-2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{4-2x-2\\cdot 1}{3-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{4-2x-2}{3-2}=2-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(2-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4-3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "731aa6f4-9b42-511b-99eb-f375784ef6ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531119} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c17466c-b8ca-50c3-9f75-a6a53610a6c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d00d5e-9f6b-5691-9183-ca640417b15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530951} :answer-field/id #uuid "79975f54-a6ab-5d67-8f15-fd4af267d146" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e73d348-8d9b-5a9f-8dbf-5305290f7f53" :question/math-academy-id "q-332913" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-3{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ -3\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-3a \\\\ -3b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2b \\\\ 2a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-3a \\\\ -3b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2b+1 \\\\ 2a+5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2b+1=-3a \\\\ 2a+5=-3b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n-2b+1=-3a\\,⇒\\,a=\\frac{2b-1}{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\frac{2b-1}{3}\\right)+5=-3b\\,⇒\\,4b-2+15=-9b\\,⇒\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\na=\\frac{2(-1)-1}{3}=\\frac{-2-1}{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76419d8d-c305-5619-a8a2-c0287e5dda0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531126} :answer-field/id #uuid "2933141c-2169-5b87-8fb5-b8ed2e025c9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cafae102-8ddc-57ce-b89b-eb060527e40e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531288} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f12c9a5-b2a0-5f55-8200-bc2b6ab50775" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d157cb9-9968-5484-a3c7-ab43310ab864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531202}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531202} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3dc74ec-4f14-5ce0-aef2-9920a7e3da3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3234de52-8801-51a2-806f-23f965c5de2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-333012" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n$2$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    .\n  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n$1$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-({a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}) \\\\ {a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-{a}_{2}+2){t}^{2}+(-{b}_{2}+1)t+(-{c}_{2}+3) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-1){t}^{2}+({b}_{1}+2)t+{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coefficients of like powers of $t,$ we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{2}+2=0 \\\\ -\\,{b}_{2}+1=2{a}_{1} \\\\ -\\,{c}_{2}+3={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1}-1=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}+2=2{a}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first and fourth equations, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2,\\,{a}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the second and fifth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=-1,\\,{b}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these last values into the third and sixth equations, and solving for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=1,\\,{c}_{1}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+2t-1 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}-t+1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "231f5d7d-ba14-58c8-9817-e96238be05d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530940} :answer-field/id #uuid "0975e181-89ef-5188-9ed5-faa802b35aa0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531390} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07e33b3-ea76-5f2d-8458-b5bf6baa03bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531322} :answer-field/id #uuid "304765d0-077d-5553-8e0b-02a9e5acf013" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf26826-fc27-58f2-b062-1e875c147069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530964}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530964} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b786bc-2f8e-50dc-9e4a-f05c7bbe489c" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b5958f-36f6-5197-b67d-199edfefbc79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531359} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad21e9c-b394-53e0-abac-39126c2eaed6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "858cb189-c87b-5c12-8cae-08db96e24407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531155} :answer-field/id #uuid "be99c1cf-9606-5cac-85ca-8bcf7bfdd5d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ae49c4e-218f-5613-b105-b87baac9b7d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531133} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf969b04-1973-578a-b415-7226b4cb20bd" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef96fb33-f115-54df-9b44-caf8bfa136a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531349}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531349} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1cb951-e683-519c-9741-c07df8a9e235" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2f551a-2dab-5878-8d7b-9b4786b3123a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530995}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530995} :answer-field/id #uuid "eedf4d51-ddf3-5e05-8956-364b54b00bc4" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48e63c6e-e110-5f2f-9c73-cb4374b7c6c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-332587" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-5}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-6}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-7}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-8}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-4)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+4\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\n$$\n\nwhere $$\n\\displaystyle x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae3f5928-02ba-596c-85cb-7d15890d6276" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531242}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531242} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cbb24e4-e2ab-54ec-bf66-effde280b307" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92982e2f-61eb-50b9-809b-23ee5a048d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531180} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cadcc96-5961-586a-8a05-aa4c6a2de9f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a525e594-c221-5dcc-979b-ca3551e65f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531220}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531220} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f7c1dd5-f9b0-5de5-b21c-aa047db00ae5"